  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The state of Arizona recorded $98.4M in federal contract obligations for FY2027 to date. The state recorded 481 awards with an average award size of $204K. Obligations fell 99.7% year over year. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $86.2M, making the Department of Veterans Affairs the dominant buyer so far this fiscal year. FEDEX SUPPLY CHAIN DISTRIBUTION SYSTEM, INC. is the top vendor with $13.8M in obligations, followed by AMERICAN VETERAN CONTRACTING SOLUTIONS LLC at $7.3M and FEDERAL EXPRESS CORPORATION at $7.1M. All Other Business Support Services is the largest industry by obligations at $13.9M, with Couriers and Express Delivery Services at $8.4M and Ambulance Services at $7.7M. Fiscal-year history shows obligations of $15.3B in FY22, $19.8B in FY23, $18B in FY24, $23.7B in FY25, and $31B in FY26. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated is federal buying in Arizona this fiscal year?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer with $86.2M in obligations. The next largest buyers are the Department of Justice with $3.6M and the Department of Health and Human Services with $3.1M. The top three agencies account for most of the $98.4M total obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which contractors and industries lead federal spending in Arizona?",
        "body": "FEDEX SUPPLY CHAIN DISTRIBUTION SYSTEM, INC. leads vendors with $13.8M in obligations, followed by AMERICAN VETERAN CONTRACTING SOLUTIONS LLC at $7.3M and FEDERAL EXPRESS CORPORATION at $7.1M. All Other Business Support Services leads industries with $13.9M, followed by Couriers and Express Delivery Services at $8.4M and Ambulance Services at $7.7M."
      }
    ]
  },
